id: pm-csv-bwrv
title: Apply edited spreadsheet exports without overwriting concurrent tracker changes
description: Export an explicit item/revision/field-digest edit session and import the edited table as a three-way patch. Reuse keyed identity and existing atomic compensation; this is distinct from the general terminal keyed retry defect and does not replace the SDK transaction coordinator.
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: added,concurrency,csv
created_at: "2026-10-21T20:06:53.134Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T20:29:31.454Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Two editors on one exported table cannot overwrite newer tracker values; terminal keyed updates stay idempotent; a stale digest causes zero item/history writes; typed SDK and CLI with compact TOON/JSON receipts and actionable refusals; documented example and real public-tracker copy validation without git; targeted regression revert proof and unchanged npm/Bun CI release gates
comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T20:07:08.204Z",codex-agent,"Overlap check against current CLI source and fleet sibling documentation: native bulk keyed upsert and workspace transactions already exist; pm-csv keyed identity, atomic coordinator integration and full-document compensation are reused. pm-ado has remote revision-checked three-way sync specific to Azure. pm-beads, pm-todos, pm-jira and pm-linear have format/service round trips, without a spreadsheet edit-session contract. No matching CSV session item found by context/search/open inventory. pm-csv-0rvm remains the separate legacy terminal retry bug. Reconciliation PR 178 closes unrelated delivered items; none will be edited. Registry latest CLI is 2026.10.21; repository pin remains unchanged."
  "2026-10-21T20:13:38.356Z",codex-agent,"Implemented versioned CSV plus baseline session JSON, explicit stable item/history/field digests, bounded typed refusals, three-way scalar patches and per-item locked conflict checks. Uses the existing SDK coordinator plus CSV full-document compensation. Ten targeted real non-git tracker scenarios pass, including two editors, zero-write stale preflight, terminal identity/lifecycle preservation, convergent retry, native-writer races and interrupted resume. Status is intentionally read-only with a lifecycle-command remedy; editable fields and boundaries are documented. Host canonicalization trims trailing body whitespace, now normalized before comparison to preserve retry idempotency."
  "2026-10-21T20:17:51.616Z",codex-agent,"Real-data validation passed on a non-git scratch copy of public pm-csv main 1f7e523b6d5539264d3316362665506486eeea3a: 118 real items, zero enumeration warnings, 17 columns/6 editable fields; session JSON 114257 bytes and CSV 97461 bytes. Three rows across open/in-progress/terminal states applied; one concurrent unedited field survived. Retry applied zero. Four whole-corpus raw-document/history hash comparisons proved zero writes for unchanged import, retry, second-editor conflict and altered revision. Actual built CLI exported 118 items with no git executable. Full-table JSON/TOON receipts measured 89/61 bytes. Single sample took 31.32 seconds. Details: docs/spreadsheet-validation.md."
  "2026-10-21T20:18:51.013Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: replaced only conflicts() with an empty conflict list, then ran node --test --test-name-pattern=\"two editors|native writer after preflight\" test/roundtrip.test.ts. Both selected regressions failed (0 pass, 2 fail, exit 1) because expected conflict refusals disappeared. Restored the function byte-for-byte. With the guard restored the targeted suite passes 12/12, and roundtrip.ts measures 100% lines, 100% branches and 100% functions under targeted V8 coverage. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings and duplication checks pass. Full unchanged npm/Bun release gates will run in CI."
  "2026-10-21T20:20:54.652Z",codex-agent,"Final targeted suite now passes 13/13 through the PM-linked runner. Added a native-convergence receipt regression: applied counts only rows actually mutated during this attempt, including zero when a native writer supplies the desired value after preflight. Local typecheck/test-typecheck/lint/docstring/duplication checks pass. Test-result tracking is disabled by existing project policy, so the linked runner printed success without persisting a run record; this comment records its 13 pass / 0 fail / 0 skip result. No tracker policy was changed."
  "2026-10-21T20:29:19.136Z",codex-agent,"CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-csv/actions/runs/39669745243 passed on implementation head 5a7d03c526ee7081e2dea78601063f40d39affb2: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed 300/300 tests on Node 22 and Node 26, with zero fail/skip/cancel/todo. All four gate executions report four required source files and 100% lines/branches/functions at unchanged thresholds; packed npm-current, bun-current and npm-minimum scenarios pass. CI strict tracker health passes. This is script-runner/Bun-launcher evidence, not a forced native-Bun claim for every test."
  "2026-10-21T20:29:23.737Z",codex-agent,"Final review cleanup replaces an array used only for its length with a numeric row counter (DeepScan USELESS_ARRAY). The SDK also refuses non-array/non-string table input as csv_edit_invalid and clones the validated baseline to prevent caller alias mutation. Typecheck, test typecheck and lint pass; affected receipt/recovery checks pass 3/3, malformed-input checks pass 2/2. A final-head CI rerun will verify the resulting commit. Review availability is separate: CodeRabbit skipped automatic review, Sourcery reported quota exhaustion, Greptile reported an expired trial, and cubic skipped. No bot was mentioned or manually triggered."
  "2026-10-21T20:29:27.633Z",codex-agent,"Implementation and evidence are ready for orchestrator verification in PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-csv/pull/179. Releasing the implementation claim; the item remains in progress and must not be closed by this agent. Final-head CI status and run counts will be recorded in the PR after the cleanup commit passes. Limits: status is read-only; hosted Postgres/MCP acceptance is unmeasured; late transaction failures require reconciliation when guarded compensation cannot safely restore."
